<title>JAPAN: Stable share volume a comfort to Japan economy-MOF.</title>
<headline>Stable share volume a comfort to Japan economy-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The recent growth and stabilisation of traded volume on Tokyo's stock exchange are helping to create a sense of stability for the economy as a whole, Vice Finance Minister Tadashi Ogawa told reporters on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Overall, the volume of traded shares has stabilised and has grown,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Such stability gives a sense of comfort for the economy as a whole,&quot; he added. &quot;Share prices are being formed in that environment.&quot;</p>
</text>
